R-DeskWay for riscv64 -- the headless build
===========================================

This build has everything unattended access needs: the root service captures
the screen through DRM/KMS (no consent dialog, login screen included), talks
to the ID server and relay, and takes keyboard and mouse input. It has no
settings window, because there is no Flutter engine for riscv64 at the Flutter
version RustDesk is built with. Set it up from a shell instead.

The service starts when the package is installed. Then, as root:

  sudo rustdesk --get-id                  this machine's ID
  sudo rustdesk --password 'SECRET'       the permanent password peers use

To use your own RustDesk server rather than the public one:

  sudo rustdesk --option custom-rendezvous-server your.server.example
  sudo rustdesk --option key 'SERVER-PUBLIC-KEY'
  sudo rustdesk --option relay-server your.server.example     (optional)
  sudo rustdesk --option api-server https://your.server.example  (optional)

`sudo rustdesk --option NAME` with no value prints the current setting.

Needs, like the other R-DeskWay packages: a Wayland (or X11) session, and an
active display output (a monitor, an HDMI dummy plug, or a forced kernel
mode) -- DRM capture reads the scanout, and a headless board has none.

The service is `rustdesk.service` (systemctl status rustdesk); logs are in
/root/.local/share/logs/RustDesk and ~/.local/share/logs/RustDesk.
